build_*/

# ring item: the Jaguar controller is an ORIGINAL model (no disc content),
# so unlike every other *_geom/_atlas blob it ships with the repo.
!ctrl_geom.bin
!ctrl_atlas.bin
mrt_gunanim.h

# Generated by the extractor from the user's disc (this repo ships no game data).
# gym_bear.h/gym_lplanes.h appeared when Lara's Home extraction was revived;
# mrt_sect.bin.prepatch is the boundary-patch backup. All three are rebuilt by
# tools/build_cof.sh, so committing them would ship level data AND go stale.
gym_bear.h
gym_lplanes.h
*.prepatch

# ☠️ DISC-DERIVED — NEVER COMMIT (purged from history 2026-08-19, user's call)
# Everything below is transcoded or extracted from the user's own Tomb Raider
# disc: the four FMV clips are Eidos/Core footage, the loading screens are PS1
# art, and the mrt_* headers are the game's models and textures. The whole
# point of tools/build_cof.sh (and the Docker image) is that a user supplies
# their own disc and the payload is generated locally. None of it belongs in a
# public repo - 43 MB across 60 blobs was on github.com/bslop/tr1-jaguar until
# it was removed.
*.JV
*.RAW
*.PCM
CAVSLOAD.BIN
CAVSLOAD.DAT
GYMLOAD.BIN
GYMLOAD.DAT
mrt_bat.h
mrt_bear.h
mrt_door.h
mrt_entex.h
mrt_gun.h
mrt_lplanes.h
mrt_pick.h
mrt_wolf.h
